<title>MEXICO: Trading in Mexican derivatives delayed.</title>
<headline>Trading in Mexican derivatives delayed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The opening of the planned Mexican Derivatives Market (Mexder) will be delayed until November 21 due to a greater demand to take part in the trading, officials said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>That means the trading floor will have to be redesigned, they said.</p>
<p>Trading was originally meant to start October 20.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728 7902))</p>
